(ned ROTARY ZERO -- find the B chuck axis from a round bar, and say how straight)
(it is. Operator 2026-08-11: "3 touches as i described. then, go +300mm in Y,)
(and 3 more touches" ... "report how accurately we have the rotaries set".)
(ONE STATION gives a datum. TWO give an ALIGNMENT: the same axis measured at two)
(Y stations 300mm apart, so the difference IS the tilt of the chuck axis against)
(the machine, in both planes at once -- dX/dY is yaw, dZ/dY is droop. A single)
(station cannot see either, and would hand back a confident datum for an axis)
(that is pointing somewhere else entirely.)
(THE DATUM IS SET FROM STATION 1 and the tool is returned there, so the number)
(on the DRO always refers to a place you can point at.)
(Z IS NOT A MIDPOINT: only the crown is reachable, so the axis is one bar RADIUS)
(below the top touch. The bar diameter is therefore the one number this routine)
(must be told, and a wrong one puts Z0 out by half the error, silently.)
(PROBE CIRCUIT. G38 reads motion.probe-input = the toolsetter contact, 7I84)
(input-28 via R10, coil between +24V and node *87, return to chassis ground)
(through the spindle -- docs/tracing/relays.md:270-278. Operator 2026-08-11:)
(the bar is electrically identical to the toolsetter, i.e. it sits on *87.)
(The M66 gate below proves the circuit is OPEN before anything commits: an)
(already-made contact is indistinguishable from an instant trip, and G38.2)
(would hand back the start point as a touch.)
o<rotary_zero> sub
  (ARG LINES ARE A CONTRACT WITH THE GUI. SubCallButton parses exactly this)
  (shape -- name, #N, then a bracketed default -- and for each one it hunts the)
  (whole app for a widget of the same name to take the value from, falling back)
  (to the default here. No widget and no default and it refuses to call at all,)
  (so every argument carries a default even though the body also treats 0 as)
  (one: the GUI never gets to send an empty field.)
  #<bar_dia> = #1 (=31.75 bar diameter mm - 1.25in)
  #<depth>   = #2 (=25.4 flank probe depth below the crown mm - 1in)
  #<yspan>   = #3 (=300.0 distance to the second station mm)
  #<max_z>   = #4 (=40.0 max search down mm)
  #<max_x>   = #5 (=40.0 max search sideways mm)
  #<f_fast>  = #6 (=100.0 find feed mm/min)
  #<f_slow>  = #7 (=10.0 latch feed mm/min)
  #<f_trav>  = #8 (=500.0 traverse feed mm/min)
  #<clear>   = #9 (=3.0 retract/clearance mm)
  o10 if [#<bar_dia> LE 0]
    #<bar_dia> = 31.75
  o10 endif
  o11 if [#<depth> LE 0]
    #<depth> = 25.4
  o11 endif
  o12 if [#<yspan> EQ 0]
    #<yspan> = 300.0
  o12 endif
  o13 if [#<max_z> LE 0]
    #<max_z> = 40.0
  o13 endif
  o14 if [#<max_x> LE 0]
    #<max_x> = 40.0
  o14 endif
  o15 if [#<f_fast> LE 0]
    #<f_fast> = 100.0
  o15 endif
  o16 if [#<f_slow> LE 0]
    #<f_slow> = 10.0
  o16 endif
  o17 if [#<f_trav> LE 0]
    #<f_trav> = 500.0
  o17 endif
  o18 if [#<clear> LE 0]
    #<clear> = 3.0
  o18 endif
  #<r_bar> = [#<bar_dia> / 2.0]
  o20 if [#5400 LE 0]
    (abort, ROTARY ZERO: no tool in the spindle - it is the probe here)
  o20 endif
  #<t_dia> = #5410
  o21 if [#<t_dia> LE 0]
    (abort, ROTARY ZERO: tool #5400 has no diameter in the table)
  o21 endif
  o22 if [#<depth> GE #<bar_dia>]
    (abort, ROTARY ZERO: probe depth is at or below the bottom of the bar)
  o22 endif
  (HALF-WIDTH AT THE PROBE DEPTH, not the radius: the flanks are touched below)
  (the crown, where the bar is narrower. 12.700mm for a 1.25in bar at 1in down.)
  #<h> = [SQRT[[#<r_bar> * #<r_bar>] - [[#<r_bar> - #<depth>] * [#<r_bar> - #<depth>]]]]
  o23 if [#<h> LE 0]
    (abort, ROTARY ZERO: probe depth gives no material to touch)
  o23 endif
  M66 P2 L0
  o90 if [#5399 LT 0]
    (abort, ROTARY ZERO: cannot read the probe input)
  o90 endif
  G92.1
  G90
  #<y0> = #5421
  (STATION 1 -- three touches where the operator parked the tool)
  (PRINT, ROTARY ZERO: station 1 at Y%.3f#<y0>)
  o<rotary_station> call [#<t_dia>] [#<depth>] [#<h>] [#<max_z>] [#<max_x>] [#<f_fast>] [#<f_slow>] [#<f_trav>] [#<clear>]
  #<z1>  = #<_rz_ztop>
  #<xl1> = #<_rz_xleft>
  #<xr1> = #<_rz_xright>
  #<xa1> = [[#<xl1> + #<xr1>] / 2.0]
  #<za1> = [#<z1> - #<r_bar>]
  (SPAN CHECK, per station. A flank that landed on a jaw, the fixture or a burr)
  (reads as a plausible number and poisons every job after it.)
  #<sp1> = [#<xr1> - #<xl1> - #<t_dia>]
  o60 if [ABS[#<sp1> - [#<h> * 2.0]] GT 1.0]
    (abort, ROTARY ZERO: station 1 flanks %.3f#<sp1> apart, expected %.3f#<h> doubled - nothing set)
  o60 endif
  (STATION 2 -- same three touches, yspan away. Lift clear before travelling.)
  G1 Z[#<z1> + #<clear>] F[#<f_trav>]
  G1 Y[#<y0> + #<yspan>] F[#<f_trav>]
  (PRINT, ROTARY ZERO: station 2 at Y%.3f#5421)
  o<rotary_station> call [#<t_dia>] [#<depth>] [#<h>] [#<max_z>] [#<max_x>] [#<f_fast>] [#<f_slow>] [#<f_trav>] [#<clear>]
  #<z2>  = #<_rz_ztop>
  #<xl2> = #<_rz_xleft>
  #<xr2> = #<_rz_xright>
  #<xa2> = [[#<xl2> + #<xr2>] / 2.0]
  #<za2> = [#<z2> - #<r_bar>]
  #<sp2> = [#<xr2> - #<xl2> - #<t_dia>]
  o61 if [ABS[#<sp2> - [#<h> * 2.0]] GT 1.0]
    (abort, ROTARY ZERO: station 2 flanks %.3f#<sp2> apart, expected %.3f#<h> doubled - nothing set)
  o61 endif
  (ALIGNMENT. dX/dY is yaw, dZ/dY is droop. Reported three ways because none of)
  (them alone is readable: raw mm over the span says how bad it is HERE, mm/m)
  (scales it to any length, and arc-minutes is what a machinist squares to.)
  #<dx> = [#<xa2> - #<xa1>]
  #<dz> = [#<za2> - #<za1>]
  #<dxm> = [#<dx> * 1000.0 / #<yspan>]
  #<dzm> = [#<dz> * 1000.0 / #<yspan>]
  (ATAN[y]/[x] is the two-argument form and returns DEGREES. Split from the)
  (x60 so no reader -- or parser -- has to reason about precedence between the)
  (slash that belongs to ATAN and a multiply that does not.)
  #<axdeg> = [ATAN[#<dx>] / [#<yspan>]]
  #<azdeg> = [ATAN[#<dz>] / [#<yspan>]]
  #<axmin> = [#<axdeg> * 60.0]
  #<azmin> = [#<azdeg> * 60.0]
  #<taper> = [[#<sp2> - #<sp1>] * 1000.0 / #<yspan>]
  (PRINT, ROTARY ZERO: station 1 axis X%.4f#<xa1> Z%.4f#<za1> crown %.4f#<z1>)
  (PRINT, ROTARY ZERO: station 2 axis X%.4f#<xa2> Z%.4f#<za2> crown %.4f#<z2>)
  (PRINT, ROTARY ALIGNMENT over %.1f#<yspan> mm of Y:)
  (PRINT,   YAW   dX = %.4f#<dx> mm  =  %.3f#<dxm> mm/m  =  %.2f#<axmin> arcmin)
  (PRINT,   DROOP dZ = %.4f#<dz> mm  =  %.3f#<dzm> mm/m  =  %.2f#<azmin> arcmin)
  (PRINT,   bar taper/runout in the span check: %.3f#<taper> mm/m)
  (PRINT,   NOTE both include the bar itself - a bent or tapered bar reads as)
  (PRINT,   misalignment. Rotate B 180 and re-run: real misalignment keeps its)
  (PRINT,   sign, bar error flips. That is the only way to tell them apart.)
  (BACK TO STATION 1 and set the datum there. Lift first.)
  G1 Z[#<z2> + #<clear>] F[#<f_trav>]
  G1 Y[#<y0>] F[#<f_trav>]
  G10 L20 P0 X[#5420 - #<xa1>] Z[#5422 - #<za1>]
  (PRINT, ROTARY ZERO: X0 Z0 now sit on the B centreline at station 1, bar %.3f#<bar_dia> dia)
o<rotary_zero> endsub
M2 (end program)
